Package: kali-rdp-kit
Version: 0.1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: ashvani <dpac9525@gmail.com>
Depends: bash (>= 5.0), xrdp, tigervnc-standalone-server, procps, iproute2
Recommends: tmux
Suggests: openbox
Homepage: https://github.com/ashvani/kali-rdp-kit
Description: Reliable headless RDP setup for Kali Linux
 Configures and repairs xrdp on Kali, where the usual Xorg backend cannot be
 used because the xorgxrdp driver is absent from the archive.
 .
 Ships three tools:
  * kali-rdp-setup   -- idempotent configuration: disables the competing
    display manager, forces the Xvnc backend, and sets a disconnected-session
    policy so abandoned sessions do not accumulate.
  * kali-rdp-doctor  -- read-only diagnostics that name the specific
    misconfiguration and the command that fixes it.
  * kali-rdp-cleanup -- reaps orphaned Xvnc, xrdp-chansrv and pipewire-xrdp
    processes, keyed on whether an RDP client is attached rather than on
    process uptime, so sessions in active use are never killed.
